WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.420
Since it premiered on HBO in the spring of
2011, Game of Thrones has become a worldwide

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:05.920
smash.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:10.700
Many stars of the show have skyrocketed to
fame, but over the course of making the series,

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.220
they've also encountered some unexpected hardships.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.740
Here's a look at some scary, tricky, and grueling
sacrifices actors had to make for Game of

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:19.240
Thrones.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:25.620
In her years of playing Sansa Stark, Sophie
Turner has endured arranged marriages, sexual

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.660
violence, and the loss of loved ones.

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:33.100
Though Sansa began the show as a spoiled child
who wanted nothing more than to be a princess,

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.780
she has grown into a shrewd warrior.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:39.860
Turner hasn't personally been through the
horrors that Sansa has, but she's endured

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:43.880
her fair share of difficulties, including
an unhygienic request.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:49.420
After Sansa escaped from King's Landing, Turner
was asked to stop washing her hair so she

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.700
would look as disheveled as possible during
Sansa's darkest times.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.760
It wasn't an enjoyable experience for Turner.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:56.300
She said:

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:57.640
"It was really disgusting.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:01.380
Now I wear a wig so I can wash my hair whenever
I want, which is nice.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:04.700
But yes, for a couple of years I was living
with pretty greasy hair."

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:09.920
One of the show's all-time hardest scenes
to watch has to be the Red Wedding near the

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:10.920
end of the third season.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:16.300
Robb Stark betrays his promise to marry the
daughter of one of his allies, Walder Frey.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:21.480
So the Freys slaughter Robb, his pregnant
bride Talisa, and his mother Catelyn.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.140
None of the actors involved in the Red Wedding
were particularly excited about filming the

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:30.260
sequence, but Oona Chaplin, who played Talisa,
had it really bad.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:35.100
After her pregnant character is repeatedly
stabbed in the stomach, she's left on the

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.700
floor to torment Robb.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:40.760
Chaplin spent hours laying on a floor in a
cold Belfast studio.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:45.240
She was "freezing" and covered in fake blood,
while she waited for the rest of the cast

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.500
to finish their scenes.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:48.580
Chaplin's commitment can't be understated.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:53.860
In the seventh season of Game of Thrones,
several characters who hadn't yet met came

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:55.520
together, with varying results.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:00.600
When Daenerys Targaryen met Jaime Lannister
for the first time, it didn't go very well.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:05.139
During their battle, Bronn, Jaime's
right hand man, must operate an enormous spear

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:08.140
launcher to fight against Daenerys' dragon,
Drogon.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:13.680
Though Bronn does get one good hit in against
Drogon, the machine is quickly burned to ashes.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.520
Bronn survives, but gets caught in the flames.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:20.740
Drogon spends most of the scene setting fire
to the battlefield.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:26.180
All the actors had to contend with smoke inhalation,
but Jerome Flynn, who plays Bronn, got the

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:26.680
worst of it.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:32.220
Director of photography Robert MacLachlan
burned diesel oil for dramatic black smoke.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.860
Most of the crew wore masks.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:39.140
Flynn had to go unmasked, and it's hard to
miss the discomfort visible on his face.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:44.739
The Battle of the Bastards, which took place
during the show's sixth season, was the culmination

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.320
of a long chain of events.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:52.040
That included Jon Snow's reunion with his
sister Sansa, her escape from her sociopathic

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:56.020
husband Ramsay Bolton, and the long-awaited
showdown among them all.

00:02:56.269 --> 00:03:01.680
As with many battles on Game of Thrones, each
moment is more brutal than the last, and throughout

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.220
the fight, it seems unlikely that Jon Snow
will emerge victorious.

00:03:05.569 --> 00:03:10.600
At one point, he ends up submerged in a pile
of dead bodies and living soldiers, gasping

00:03:10.609 --> 00:03:15.439
for breath as he struggles to rise to the
surface, which reportedly terrified actor

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:17.300
Kit Harington, who plays Snow.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.040
He didn't enjoy this part of filming, as being
crushed is one of his biggest fears.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:26.040
He gave up his own comfort to create a singular
moment for viewers.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:32.460
Speaking of Ramsay Bolton, when viewers met
the character, played by Iwan Rheon in season

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.880
three, he was a bastard, much like Jon Snow.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:39.959
When he helped his father, Roose Bolton, secure
the North, he was made an official Bolton

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:40.700
in his own right.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:46.459
After watching Ramsay generally be the worst
person of all time, fans were thrilled when

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:50.460
Ramsay met a bitter and bloody end in the
aftermath of the Battle of the Bastards.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:56.180
It was especially satisfying to hear him being
torn apart by his own pack of angry attack

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:56.680
dogs.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.860
"They’re loyal beasts."

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:00.520
"They were.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.200
Now they’re starving."

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:08.599
But before that goes down, once the larger
battle ends, Jon and Ramsay find themselves

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.780
back at Winterfell ready to keep fighting.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:14.440
Jon snaps and brutally beats Ramsay into submission.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:19.080
However, some of this ended up becoming a
reality for Rheon, who was actually punched

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.940
in the face twice by Harington.

00:04:21.329 --> 00:04:25.860
Harington said Rheon was extremely nice about
the situation, but it's unlikely that Rheon

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.320
was thrilled about taking two for the team.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:34.620
Since debuting on the show during season two,
Brienne of Tarth, played by actress Gwendoline

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:40.210
Christie, has won audiences' hearts with her
fierce battle skills, unerring loyalty, and

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.080
quick quips.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:47.120
After serving a few fallen characters including
Catelyn Stark, Brienne strikes up a real friendship

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.280
with Jaime Lannister.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:53.540
Between her bond with the Kingslayer and her
continued devotion to Catelyn, Brienne has

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:54.820
become a fan favorite.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:05:00.140
As such, fans are always frightened when Brienne
ends up in a life-threatening situation.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:05.840
When Brienne and Jaime are captured and held
hostage by Locke, a hunter for House Bolton,

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:11.181
Locke forces Brienne to face down a real bear
in a fighting pit, causing Jaime to jump in

00:05:11.181 --> 00:05:11.840
and rescue her.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.700
Although Christie said the bear was a "diva,"
requiring its own trailer, she also said that

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:20.820
it was terrifying to face down the giant animal
with nothing more than an electric fence between

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:21.320
them.

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:22.280
"And you believed them?"

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:24.020
"Why do you think I look so scared?"

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:31.920
Few of Thrones' villains have elicited a public
reaction quite as visceral as Joffrey Baratheon,

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:34.840
the sadistic eldest son of Cersei Lannister.

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:41.800
A bitter, violence-hungry child born of incest,
King Joffrey's vengeful and ill-advised decision

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:47.080
to execute Ned Stark in the show's first season
set off most of the entire story's conflict.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:51.700
"So long as I am your king, treason shall
never go unpunished.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:56.180
Ser Ilyn, bring me his head!"

00:05:56.360 --> 00:06:00.979
Viewers have watched him murder prostitutes
sex workers, threaten to beat women, and verbally

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:02.300
abuse pretty much everyone.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:06.260
It's no wonder viewers loved watching Joffrey
get slapped.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:10.320
He meets an extremely ugly end early in the
fourth season.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:16.759
During his wedding to Margaery Tyrell, Joffrey
takes a final sip of wine, gruesomely choking

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:18.420
to death in front of the entire court.

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:22.320
Actor Jack Gleeson quit acting after his last
moments as Joffrey.

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:27.100
He said that aside from the choking itself,
keeping his eyes open was the hardest part.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:32.160
They actually had to be held open so he didn't
blink, making filming the scene that much

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.160
more uncomfortable.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:38.600
Cersei Lannister, yet another Thrones character
that viewers love to hate, has committed her

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.340
fair share of atrocities.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:46.160
Y'know, stuff like enabling her evil son Joffrey,
carrying on a decades-long affair with her

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.600
twin brother, and slaughtering most of King's
Landing by burning them with wildfire.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:55.280
She got her just desserts for some of her
crimes at the end of the show's fifth season,

00:06:55.280 --> 00:07:00.620
when she was forced to take a walk of atonement
through King's Landing completely naked while

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:03.480
the townspeople verbally and physically abused
her.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:07.780
The walk was shot in Dubrovnik,
Croatia  near an ancient church.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:11.380
The production was nearly banned, however,
due to the nudity.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:15.100
In the end, actress Lena Headey asked for
a body double.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:20.840
Thanks to the magic of visual effects, Rebecca
Van Cleave's body stood in for Cersei's.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:26.520
Van Cleave spent three days walking the streets
of Dubrovnik completely naked while crew members

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:28.740
and extras shouted and pelted her with food.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:31.000
Van Cleave’s face was never shown.

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:37.020
After a number of shocking deaths throughout
Thrones' run, viewers have accepted the idea

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:42.360
that nobody is safe, which made Jon Snow's
false start of a death all the more horrifying.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:48.300
During the season five finale, Jon, now the
Lord Commander of the Night's Watch, is betrayed

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:52.060
by his men and repeatedly stabbed over accusations
of treason.

00:07:52.469 --> 00:07:57.880
The show cuts to black, leaving anxious fans
without answers regarding Jon's fate until

00:07:57.880 --> 00:07:59.080
the next season premiere.

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:04.320
Actor Kit Harington told various media outlets
he would not be returning to the show, which

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:06.520
turned out to be a pretty enormous lie.

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:10.000
Jon was alive and well by the second episode
of the next season.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:12.180
Harington reportedly hated lying.

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:17.830
With huge fans like President Barack Obama
concerned about Jon Snow's fate, Harington

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:20.380
had to play it extremely safe for over a year.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:25.150
He did get himself out of a speeding ticket
by revealing one of the show's biggest spoilers

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:30.300
to an anxious police officer, so at least
there was one silver lining to this sacrifice.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:37.160
"I looked at him and went, 'I’m alive next
season,' and he goes, he says, 'Mmm-hmm.

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:39.880
On your way, Lord Commander.'"

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:45.920
Throughout Game of Thrones' run, Arya Stark
has transformed from a young, impetuous would-be

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:49.120
warrior to a truly dangerous faceless assassin.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:53.600
After watching her father's public execution
and making the journey from Westeros

00:08:53.601 --> 00:08:58.640
to the House of the Undying in Braavos,
she agrees to learn from the mysterious face-changer

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:00.120
Jaqen H'ghar.

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:04.200
She waits outside the House for days to earn
her place inside.

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:10.240
As soon as Arya learns how to change faces,
she uses her power to kill Meryn Trant.

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:16.340
Because it wasn't yet Meryn's turn to die,
Arya is punished by Jaqen, who blinds her

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:18.080
and forces her to live as a beggar.

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:20.720
While blind, Arya's eyes are clouded.

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:27.400
Unfortunately for actress Maisie Williams,
her contacts were quite thick and hand-painted,

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.860
actually obscuring her vision.

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:33.750
Williams admitted that while she didn't want
to complain, her blind scenes left her in

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:35.220
a significant amount of pain.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:40.740
She stuck with it, ensuring that each shot
during Arya's blind phase was exactly right.

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:46.960
Theon Greyjoy, the once cocky heir to the
Iron Islands, has been through his fair share

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:47.740
of ordeals.

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:54.000
Once a young, stubborn ward of the North,
Theon was initially loyal to Robb Stark in

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.260
the wake of Ned's death.

00:09:55.770 --> 00:10:01.200
Eventually, he betrayed Robb and was captured
by the sadistic Ramsay Bolton, who physically

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:05.880
and psychologically destroyed Theon until
he referred to himself as "Reek."

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:10.890
Perhaps the hardest scenes for actor Alfie
Allen to endure throughout Thrones were his

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:12.520
torture scenes with Ramsay.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:17.480
He spent most of a full season strung up,
savagely mutilated and beaten.

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:22.400
It can't have been easy for Allen to even
pretend to be tortured, and he has since spoken

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:23.980
out about how hard it was to play.

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:28.990
He watched movies that prominently featured
torture, including Quentin Tarantino's bloody

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:30.660
classic Reservoir Dogs.

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:35.440
Spending so much time working within this
unflinchingly terrible part of Theon's story

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:37.540
must have been incredibly difficult for Allen.

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:42.460
Some viewers might have forgotten about Lancel
Lannister, played by Eugene Simon.

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:47.780
When audiences meet a younger Lancel, he is
a seemingly innocent squire to King Robert

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:49.040
until the monarch's death.

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:53.840
After an ill-advised affair with his cousin
Cersei, which is somehow not the grossest

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:59.630
relationship she has in the show, Lancel is
severely wounded in season two's Battle of

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:02.180
Blackwater Bay and shunted to the sidelines.

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:08.520
When Lancel returns, he's joined an oppressive
and severe religious sect called the Sparrows.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:13.840
When Lancel spills the beans about his relationship
with Cersei, she gets angrier than ever.

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:19.280
Rather than attend her own trial, the vengeful
Queen Mother unleashes a magical wildfire

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:21.940
throughout King's Landing, killing numerous
people.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:26.800
Lancel, sent to find the missing Cersei during
her trial, discovers her plan.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:30.740
He can't stop the explosion in time, despite
his best efforts.

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:37.090
Simon spent hours crawling through a dark
dungeon, enduring the journey a whopping 27

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:38.480
times until they got the shot right.

